# Deploy target — DigitalOcean Kubernetes (DOKS)

Provisions the managed cluster `deploy/chart/` installs into. State
is remote in a Spaces bucket (binding spec §5); one state per
environment via workspaces. Credentials ride the environment, never
a file:

```sh
export DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN=…        # API token, read by both configs
export SPACES_ACCESS_KEY_ID=…      # Spaces key, for the bootstrap config
export SPACES_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=…
export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID="$SPACES_ACCESS_KEY_ID"          # the same key,
export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="$SPACES_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY"  # for the S3 state backend
```

## Once per project

```sh
./bootstrap.sh    # provisions the state bucket, then `tofu init`
```

The bootstrap config keeps local state on purpose — the bucket is the
one resource that cannot live inside the remote state it hosts.
Commit `bootstrap/terraform.tfstate`; it contains no secrets.

## Per environment

```sh
tofu workspace new dev    # once per environment; `tofu workspace select` thereafter
tofu apply
```

## Deploying

The release pipeline pushes the image; the chart runs it here. Config
rides `values.yaml` → container environment — one image serves every
environment:

```sh
doctl kubernetes cluster kubeconfig save "$(tofu output -raw cluster_name)"
helm upgrade --install <%= projectName %> ../../deploy/chart \
  --set image.repository=<registry>/<%= projectName %> \
  --set image.tag=v1.2.3
```
